"num_games_owned": 34, "num_reviews": 1, "playtime_forever": 186923, "playtime_last_two_weeks": 0, "playtime_at_review": 74829, "last_played": 1786847146, "avatar": "c4fc24e6378b019b5057c929ca6ead9818bb84f0"}, "language": "english", "review": "I have 1,200 hours invested into this game, and I swear this game is the most addictive thing I have played. I have gotten 1,200 hours, and I only got the game in June of 2020 (it's 3/15/2021). I spent some time with a Milsim unit and this game plus a decent map maker leads to a great immersive factor. The campaign is great to play once and never touch again, but the base game has lots of stuff for everyone to try. With very immersive Air, ground, and naval warfare, no two experiences in this game will be them. PLUS, this game has lots of mods like RHS, CUP, USAF, Ni arms, USS Nimitz, and even star wars/ Halo mods! This game will never get old!\n\nNote: Most of my time was spent with JTF-Manticore (as Medic/ Infantry/ pilot/ what ever the ♥♥♥♥ High Command told me to do lol), 107th Navy refueling (as an airedale/ MEDIVAC/ MP) Altis Warlords 1e (mostly a CAS pilot in A-10), Asylum life #1 (it's not meth, officer. i promise it's just salt), and Antistasi Altis/Takistan.\n\nWarning: this game will lead to hours of devotion, and is just as, if not more addictive than meth.", "timestamp_created": 1615838806, "timestamp_updated": 1619282816, "voted_up": true, "votes_up": 1, "votes_funny": 0, "weighted_vote_score": "0.523809552192687988", "comment_count": 1, "steam_purchase": true, "received_for_free": false, "refunded": false, "written_during_early_access": false, "primarily_steam_deck": false, "app_release_date": "1378969200", "reactions": []}]}